# Trivy Vulnerability Ignore File
# This file contains vulnerabilities that are being intentionally ignored
# Each entry should include a comment explaining why it's safe to ignore

# ==================== POLICY ====================
# GitHub workflows enforce: CRITICAL,HIGH severity only
# See: .github/actions/trivy-scan/action.yml
#
# MEDIUM and LOW severity vulnerabilities do not block CI/CD and
# should NOT be added to this file unless there is a specific reason
# to suppress them from local development scans.

# ==================== EXAMPLE FORMAT ====================
# CVE-YYYY-XXXXX - Brief description
# Affects: package-name version
# Severity: CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW
# Issue: Detailed description of vulnerability
# Risk: Analysis of actual risk in this context
# Status: Fixed in version X.Y.Z / No fix available (affected)
# Reason: Why it's safe to ignore (false positive, not applicable, etc.)
# Review: When to re-evaluate this decision
# CVE-YYYY-XXXXX

# ==================== ACTIVE IGNORES ====================

# CVE-2024-52308 - GitHub CLI SSH command injection vulnerability (FALSE POSITIVE)
# Affects: github.com/cli/cli/v2
# Severity: HIGH
# Issue: RCE via malicious Codespace SSH server when using `gh codespace ssh` or `gh codespace logs`
#        Improper validation of remote username allows command injection via SSH arguments
# Risk: This container installs gh CLI v2.83.1 (see Dockerfile line 19: ARG GH_VERSION=2.83.1)
#       CVE-2024-52308 was fixed in gh CLI v2.62.0 (released 2024-11-14)
#       Version 2.83.1 > 2.62.0, therefore not vulnerable
# Status: Fixed in version 2.62.0 (we're running 2.83.1)
# Reason: False positive - Trivy incorrectly identifies gh v2.83.1 as vulnerable
#         Possible issue: Trivy's version detection for Go binaries or stale vulnerability DB
# Review: Remove this entry when Trivy's vulnerability database is updated to correctly
#         recognize gh v2.83.1 as not vulnerable. Check Trivy release notes and test without
#         this ignore after Trivy updates. Next review: 2026-01-01
CVE-2024-52308

# CVE-2025-61729 - Golang stdlib HostnameError DoS vulnerability
# Affects: GitHub CLI with Go stdlib 1.25.3 (embedded binary dependency)
# Issue: Denial of Service via malicious TLS certificates with excessive SAN entries
# Risk: LOW - Requires MITM attack or malicious server, DoS only (no data breach)
# Status: AWAITING UPSTREAM - GitHub CLI v2.83.1 (latest) still uses Go 1.25.0
# Fixed Versions: Go 1.25.5, 1.24.11 (waiting for gh CLI v2.84.0+ release)
# Mitigation: Updated to latest available gh CLI version for incremental security improvements
# Timeline:
#   - 2025-12-05: CVE discovered in nightly Trivy scan
#   - 2025-12-05: Added to ignore list (upstream patch not yet available)
#   - Review: 2025-12-19 (check for gh CLI v2.84.0+ with Go 1.25.5)
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://github.com/cli/cli/releases
#   - Tracking issue: https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/12250
# Review: 2025-12-19
CVE-2025-61729

# CVE-2025-66564 - Sigstore Timestamp Authority DoS vulnerability
# Affects: github.com/sigstore/timestamp-authority v1.2.9 (embedded in GitHub CLI v2.83.1)
# Severity: HIGH (CVSS 7.5) - Risk downgraded to LOW in deployment context
# Issue: DoS vulnerability in timestamp-authority API server handlers
# Risk: LOW - GitHub CLI only uses client functions, not vulnerable API server code
#       Vulnerability requires running timestamp-authority as a service with untrusted input
#       gh CLI uses library for attestation verification (client-side only)
#       EPSS: 0.0004 (0.04% exploitation probability - bottom 12th percentile)
#       DoS only - no confidentiality or integrity impact
# Status: AWAITING UPSTREAM - Fixed in timestamp-authority v2.0.3 (commit 0cae34e1)
#         GitHub CLI v2.83.1 includes timestamp-authority v1.2.9
#         Waiting for gh CLI v2.84.0+ to incorporate updated dependency
# Mitigation: Running latest available gh CLI version (v2.83.1)
# Timeline:
#   - 2025-12-08: CVE discovered in nightly Trivy scan
#   - 2025-12-08: Added to ignore list (upstream patch not yet available in gh CLI)
#   - Review: 2025-12-22 (check for gh CLI v2.84.0+ with updated dependencies)
# Tracking:
#   - POA&M: .claude/context/cybersecurity/poam/poam-2025-12-08-trivy-gh-timestamp-authority.md
#   - Monitor: https://github.com/cli/cli/releases
#   - Dependency: https://github.com/sigstore/timestamp-authority/releases
# Review: 2025-12-22
CVE-2025-66564

# CVE-2026-22817, CVE-2026-22818 - Hono JWT algorithm confusion vulnerabilities
# Affects: hono@4.11.3 (transitive dependency via Claude Code or Gemini CLI in base image)
# Severity: HIGH (CVSS 8.2) - Risk downgraded to LOW in deployment context
# Issue: JWT algorithm confusion in Hono's JWT and JWK/JWKS middleware allows
#        forged token acceptance when explicit algorithm configuration is missing
# Risk: LOW - Despite HIGH severity (CVSS 8.2), vulnerable code is not executed
#       This container extends ai-assistant-home base image which provides CLI tools
#       (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Goose), NOT web services
#       - No web server or HTTP endpoints exposed
#       - No JWT token processing or authentication workflows
#       - Hono's JWT middleware is not invoked in CLI workflows
#       - Vulnerable code path is unreachable in this deployment context
#       EPSS: Not yet available (CVEs disclosed 2026-01-13)
# Status: AWAITING UPSTREAM - Fixed in hono@4.11.4+
#         Waiting for Claude Code or Gemini CLI to update their dependencies
# Mitigation: Using latest available versions of base image tools
# Fixed Versions: hono@4.11.4+
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-01-13: CVEs disclosed by Hono project
#   - 2026-01-14: Detected during nightly Trivy scan, added to ignore list
# Tracking:
#   - Base image tracking: image/.trivyignore
#   - Monitor: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@anthropic-ai/claude-code
#   - Monitor: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@google/gemini-cli
#   - GitHub Actions failure: https://github.com/rise8-us/xpai-ai-assistant-container/actions/runs/20980327903
# CVSS: 8.2 HIGH (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:N)
# CWE: CWE-347 (Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature)
# Review: Weekly until base image updates to include hono@4.11.4+
CVE-2026-22817
CVE-2026-22818

# CVE-2025-61726 - Golang net/url DoS vulnerability
# Affects: GitHub CLI with Go stdlib 1.25.3 (embedded binary dependency)
# Severity: HIGH (CVSS 7.5)
# Issue: Denial of Service via excessive URL query parameters causing memory exhaustion
#        The net/http.Request.ParseForm method processes large URL-encoded forms without
#        limits on the number of unique parameters, leading to uncontrolled memory allocation
# Risk: LOW - Requires user to explicitly invoke gh commands with malicious URLs
#       - No automatic URL processing or network listeners
#       - CLI tool usage pattern limits exposure to untrusted input
#       - DoS only (no confidentiality or integrity impact)
#       - Container usage: developer workstation, not internet-facing service
# Status: AWAITING UPSTREAM - GitHub CLI v2.86.0 uses Go 1.25.3
# Fixed Versions: Go 1.25.6, 1.24.12 (released 2026-01-15)
#                 Waiting for gh CLI v2.87.0+ to incorporate Go 1.25.6+
# Mitigation: Upgraded to gh CLI v2.86.0 (latest available)
#             Users should only run gh commands with trusted GitHub repositories
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-01-15: Go 1.25.6 released with fix
#   - 2026-02-02: CVE discovered in nightly Trivy scan
#   - 2026-02-02: Added to ignore list (upstream patch not yet in gh CLI)
#   - 2026-02-02: Upgraded gh CLI from v2.83.1 to v2.86.0
#   - Review: 2026-02-16 (check for gh CLI with Go 1.25.6+)
# Tracking:
#   - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-61726
#   - Go Advisory: GO-2026-4341
#   - Go Issue: https://go.dev/issue/77101
#   - Go Change: CL/736712
#   - Monitor: https://github.com/cli/cli/releases
#   - POA&M: .claude/context/cybersecurity/poam/poam-2026-02-02-trivy-golang-stdlib.md
# CVSS: 7.5 HIGH (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H)
# CWE: CWE-400 (Uncontrolled Resource Consumption)
# CISA KEV: Not listed (no known active exploitation)
# Review: 2026-02-16
CVE-2025-61726

# CVE-2025-61728 - Golang archive/zip DoS vulnerability
# Affects: GitHub CLI with Go stdlib 1.25.3 (embedded binary dependency)
# Severity: HIGH (CVSS 6.5)
# Issue: Excessive CPU consumption when building archive index in archive/zip
#        Super-linear file name indexing algorithm invoked when opening ZIP files
#        Maliciously constructed archives with specific filename patterns trigger
#        computational exhaustion, causing denial of service
# Risk: LOW - Requires user to explicitly download and process malicious ZIP archives
#       - gh CLI may process ZIPs for release artifacts (`gh release download`)
#       - Primary use case: trusted GitHub.com repositories (high trust context)
#       - Requires user action (not passive background processing)
#       - DoS only (no confidentiality or integrity impact)
#       - Container usage: developer workstation, not internet-facing service
# Status: AWAITING UPSTREAM - GitHub CLI v2.86.0 uses Go 1.25.3
# Fixed Versions: Go 1.25.6, 1.24.12 (released 2026-01-15)
#                 Waiting for gh CLI v2.87.0+ to incorporate Go 1.25.6+
# Mitigation: Upgraded to gh CLI v2.86.0 (latest available)
#             Users should only download releases from trusted GitHub repositories
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-01-15: Go 1.25.6 released with fix
#   - 2026-02-02: CVE discovered in nightly Trivy scan
#   - 2026-02-02: Added to ignore list (upstream patch not yet in gh CLI)
#   - 2026-02-02: Upgraded gh CLI from v2.83.1 to v2.86.0
#   - Review: 2026-02-16 (check for gh CLI with Go 1.25.6+)
# Tracking:
#   - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-61728
#   - Go Issue: https://go.dev/issue/77102
#   - Researcher: Jakub Ciolek
#   - Monitor: https://github.com/cli/cli/releases
#   - POA&M: .claude/context/cybersecurity/poam/poam-2026-02-02-trivy-golang-stdlib.md
# CVSS: 6.5 HIGH (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H)
# CWE: CWE-407 (Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity)
# CISA KEV: Not listed (no known active exploitation)
# Review: 2026-02-16
CVE-2025-61728

# CVE-2025-61730 - Golang crypto/tls TLS 1.3 handshake info disclosure
# Affects: GitHub CLI with Go stdlib 1.25.5 (embedded binary dependency)
# Severity: HIGH
# Issue: During TLS 1.3 handshake, messages spanning encryption level boundaries
#        may be processed before encryption level changes, causing info disclosure
# Risk: LOW - Requires network-local attacker with precise timing during active
#       TLS handshake. gh CLI is user-initiated, connects to trusted GitHub endpoints.
#       No passive network listeners. Info disclosure only.
# Status: AWAITING UPSTREAM - GitHub CLI v2.86.0 uses Go 1.25.5
# Fixed Versions: Go 1.25.6, 1.24.12
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-01-28: CVE published
#   - 2026-02-10: Detected in nightly Trivy scan, added to ignore list
#   - Review: 2026-02-24 (check for gh CLI with Go 1.25.7+)
# Tracking:
#   - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-61730
#   - Go Issue: https://go.dev/issue/76443
#   - Monitor: https://github.com/cli/cli/releases
# CVSS: HIGH
# CWE: Not yet assigned
# CISA KEV: Not listed (no known active exploitation)
# Review: 2026-02-24
CVE-2025-61730

# CVE-2025-68121 - Golang crypto/tls session resumption cert validation bypass
# Affects: GitHub CLI with Go stdlib 1.25.5 (embedded binary dependency)
# Severity: HIGH (CWE-295: Improper Certificate Validation)
# Issue: During TLS session resumption, mutated ClientCAs/RootCAs between initial
#        and resumed handshake may allow sessions that should have been rejected
# Risk: LOW - Requires dynamic TLS config mutations between connections.
#       gh CLI uses standard static TLS config against github.com.
#       No Config.Clone + CA pool mutation patterns in CLI usage.
# Status: AWAITING UPSTREAM - GitHub CLI v2.86.0 uses Go 1.25.5
# Fixed Versions: Go 1.25.7, 1.24.13, 1.26.0-rc.3 (note: initial fix in 1.25.6 had regressions)
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-02-05: CVE published
#   - 2026-02-10: Detected in nightly Trivy scan, added to ignore list
#   - Review: 2026-02-24 (check for gh CLI with Go 1.25.7+)
# Tracking:
#   - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-68121
#   - Go Issue: https://go.dev/issue/77113, https://go.dev/issue/77217 (follow-up)
#   - Monitor: https://github.com/cli/cli/releases
# CVSS: HIGH
# CWE: CWE-295 (Improper Certificate Validation)
# CISA KEV: Not listed (no known active exploitation)
# Review: 2026-02-24
CVE-2025-68121

